	"pronunciation": {
		"component": "LO2Demystify",
		"content": [
			"<p>1 Silent letters at the end of a word <img src='/img/lo2/shh.jpg' style='vertical-align: middle;' alt='lady with finger to lips. Shh'/></p><p>The consonants <strong>d</strong>, <strong>g</strong>, <strong>p</strong>, <strong>s</strong>, <strong>t</strong>, <strong>x</strong>, <strong>z</strong> are silent when they are the last letter of the word. Listen to the following examples.</p><p><span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/005-grand.mp3' alt='grand'>gran<strong>d</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/015-rond.mp3' alt='rond'>ron<strong>d</strong></span>,  <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/009-long.mp3' alt='long'>lon<strong>g</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/022-trop.mp3' alt='trop'>tro<strong>p</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/vocabulary/007-depuis.mp3' alt='depuis'>depui<strong>s</strong></span>,  <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/013-pas.mp3' alt='pas'>pa<strong>s</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/014-petit.mp3' alt='petit'>peti<strong>t</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/016-salut.mp3' alt='salut'>salu<strong>t</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/004-gateaux.mp3' alt='gâteaux'>gâteau<strong>x</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/001-appelez.mp3' alt='appelez'>appele<strong>z</strong></span></p><p>The letter <strong>e</strong> is not pronounced at the end of a word:</p><p><span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/006-je-m-appelle.mp3' alt='Je m''appelle'>Je m&apos;appell<strong>e</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/vocabulary/004-bibliothecaire.mp3' alt='bibliothécaire'>bibliothécair<strong>e</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/vocabulary/005-celibataire.mp3' alt='célibataire'>célibatair<strong>e</strong></span></p><p><strong>NB</strong> 2-letter words ending in <strong>e</strong> are exceptions:</p><p><span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/002-ce.mp3'>ce</span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/003-de.mp3'>de</span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/008-je.mp3'>je</span>,  <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/grammar/grammar-and-usage/015-le.mp3'>le</span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/011-me.mp3'>me</span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/012-ne.mp3'>ne</span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/017-se.mp3'>se</span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/018-te.mp3'>te</span></p><hr/><p>2 <strong>Th</strong></p><p>In French the letters <strong>th</strong> are pronounced <strong>t</strong>. e.g. <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/021-thomas.mp3' alt='Thomas'><strong>Thomas</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/019-the.mp3' alt='thé'><strong>thé</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/020-theologie.mp3' alt='théologie'><strong>théologie</strong></span>, <span class='audio-link' sound-file='/audio/lo2/pronunciation/demystify/010-maths.mp3' alt='maths'><strong>maths</strong></span></p>"
		],
		"expandable": false,
		"id": "pronunciation",
		"menuText": "Pronunciation",
		"titleText": "Demystifying French Pronunciation"
	},
